                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Jumpfist is a hard as nails platformer akin to games like super meat boy. The objective is to get through the level dodging and/or destroying obstacles and enemies to reach your goal of collecting all of Jumpfist's games back.\n\nThe gameplay takes a bit of getting used to (such as the wall jump :P) but once you master these controls levels become a smooth platforming experience. As i said this game is HARD, but not impossible, giving you great satisfaction when you complete a level. The mechanics of punching and elbow-dropping are used well and in some clever ways to get the better of enemies and obstacles that may have previously bested you or even create quicker paths to the exit for those skilled enough ;).\n\nJumpfist was also developed by one person who taught himself to code and design from scratch using tutorials online and the help resources within Gamemaker Studio. From the code to the artwork, to even the voice acting. This is his first step into the world of game development so let's show our support; and for the price it is, showing support is easy :D.\n\nAll in all solid platforming experience, would take the Jumpfist challenge again.\n\nP.s. don't forget to GET THAT PARKOUR!!",
